# Google Sheets Sync Process

Owner invariants (tabs, projections, outbox, drain): [`sheet-sync.md`](../../docs/knowledge/services/sheet-sync.md), [`google-sheets.md`](../../docs/knowledge/services/google-sheets.md). Canonical commands: [`domain-commands.md`](../../docs/knowledge/services/domain-commands.md). Ordinary [No-Sync Lead](../../../CONTEXT.md) (`noSyncAppliesToNormalTabs` in `src/services/sheetSync/noSyncLead.ts`) skips/deletes Master Leads Forms and Calls only; [Unmatched Call Lead](../../../CONTEXT.md) stays a separate empty-plan skip (`created_on_unmatched`).

## Env, modes, quotas

- `TEST_MODE=true` reads `TEST_`-prefixed container ids through `src/config/domain/runtime.ts`.
- Container env names (`src/config/domain/sheets.ts`): `MASTER_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `MASTER_BOOKED_SHEET_ID`, `TBM_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `TBM_PRIME_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `TOP10_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `BEST_RELOCATION_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `GETMOVERS_LEADS_SHEET_ID`, `MAINSITE_LEADS_SHEET_ID`.
- `WRITE_SOURCE_LEAD_SHEETS` defaults false (`shouldWriteSourceLeadSheets()`; only literal `"true"` enables dual writes).
- `SHEET_SYNC_MODE`: `legacy` (default / unknown fallback), `queued`, `disabled` (`getSheetSyncMode()`).
- Queue publish (`shouldPublishSheetSyncQueue`): not a Vantage test runner; hosted function runtime (`VERCEL=1` plus `VERCEL_REGION`); **and** non-preview `VERCEL_ENV` (`shouldPublishSheetSyncQueue`). Preview/local never publish. `SHEET_SYNC_QUEUE_LOCAL_PUBLISH` does not enable publish. Topic `sheet-sync-events` / `sheet-sync-events-dev` (`SHEET_SYNC_QUEUE_TOPIC` override). Admin retry starts `runSheetSyncDrain("admin")` and does not publish.
- Cron: `router.all("/api/cron/sheet-sync-drain")`, auth `CRON_SECRET` (Bearer or `x-cron-secret`), no-op unless queued, every 5 minutes (`vercel.json`). Consumer: `api/queues/sheet-sync-consumer.ts` (payload ignored).
- Google hard ceilings: 60 reads/min and 60 writes/min per user. Default operational budgets 45/45 (`SHEET_SYNC_READS_PER_MINUTE_BUDGET`, `SHEET_SYNC_WRITES_PER_MINUTE_BUDGET`). Other knobs: `SHEET_SYNC_MAX_JOBS_PER_DRAIN` (500), `SHEET_SYNC_DEBOUNCE_WINDOW_MS` (3000), `SHEET_SYNC_MAX_ATTEMPTS` (8), payload/batch/lease/run-duration envs in `getSheetSyncBudgets` / `getSheetSyncDrainGuardrails`.
- Quota deferral retries in 60s and does not burn an attempt. Coalesce only `pending`/`retrying`.

## Operational safety

- Before manually changing jobs, count/group by `status`, `run_id`, `operation`, `resource`, `entity_model`, and creation window.
- Prefer `cancelled` plus a clear `last_error` over `failed` when abandoning verified backfill work.
- Never reset stuck `processing` jobs to `pending` until the underlying failure is fixed. The drainer may release leftover claims to `pending` on run timeout by design.
- After cleanup, confirm `processing` is zero and live statuses are expected.

